; $VER: Security-Startup 45.1 (28.08.2026)
;
; Run by dos.library before S:Startup-Sequence when security.library is
; part of the ROM. Remove this file to boot as a single-user system.
;
; NOTE: like the Startup-Sequence this script runs in a shell on the boot
; console; it MUST end with EndCLI, otherwise the shell stays interactive
; and the Startup-Sequence does not run until EndCLI is typed.
;
; Log in. PARENT makes the boot process inherit the login, so that the
; Startup-Sequence (and everything it starts) runs as the logged-in user.
; On an unconfigured system (no SYS:Security/passwd) this logs in as root
; without asking.
Login PARENT QUIET
;
; Per-user settings: point HOME: at the user's home directory when known.
If EXISTS SECURITY:
    If "$Home" NOT EQ ""
        Assign HOME: "$Home"
    EndIf
EndIf
EndCLI >NIL:
